  "final_unit_corrections": "The first final evaluation passed SQL comparisons and audits but one historical unit still required rejection of table-FK metadata. It was replaced with decoding and exact retained child-position/parent-target assertions. The second evaluation exposed a real comment-position regression in a proposed last-column removal rewrite. A differential reproduction fails 2/158 comparisons before restoring the existing removal algorithm. Both failed unit logs/plans/receipts and that reproduction are retained; the final source and fresh seeds are evaluated again.",
  "reference_protocol": "Both executables receive complete statements on separate input lines. Compare return codes, output, normalized diagnostics, persisted catalog/rows/rowids and integrity checks. Expected rows are never sorted or filtered to hide ordering differences.",
  "implementation_scope": "TableConstraintDef retains REFERENCES metadata. Independent token replay admits one child and one explicit/implicit parent key with immediate NO ACTION semantics, shared with column REFERENCES replay. The compiled catalog cache resolves named child positions and preserves declaration order. Schema/source construction excludes retained clauses only after validating the original declaration. ALTER rewrites child lists and preserves trailing table constraints; dropping a constrained child fails atomically with SQLite diagnostics.",
  "proof_scope": "The no-table-clause collection contract preserves the existing column declaration program, alongside retained-program equality and existing source/schema proofs. Source-free CREATE traces require neither column nor table REFERENCES. The source-aware DROP trace now starts from executeBase so its successful premise includes the new table-FK dependency validation; ordinary Core storage operations keep their existing domain. These are component/trace contracts, not a proof of complete SQLite FK equivalence.",
